WEBVTT

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.820
Why are you so jittery, Cetrano? It's just us.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.060
You know better than to jump somebody like that, Rycin.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:26.180
Just keeping you on your toes, buddy boy. I need you razor sharp.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.280
'Cause we're going tonight.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.350
Since when?

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.270
Big storm's moving in, Joey.

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:35.310
Mick says it'll make it harder for him to track us in the mud and all.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:52.280
Thank you, Mick.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:06.520
You know, we can move a whole lot faster out there without the extra baggage.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:09.980
You won't forget about it. I ain't going anywhere without Don.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:13.060
Neither are you. Unless you're planning to go after the money alone.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:17.890
I wouldn't face that damn swamp alone. A guy'd have to be nuts to try that.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:21.270
And maybe there's enough cash sitting out there to drive a guy nuts.

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:28.320
Don't be a jerk. We're in this together. Partners all the way.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.200
Out, out, out, out!

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:33.990
Move!

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:35.640
Move!

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:36.640
Damn it!

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:37.640
Come on!

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.640
I'm sorry, Mick is getting to me there!

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:40.640
Get out of there!

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:41.530
Get out!

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:42.960
Get out!

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:52.180
Get out!

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:02.600
We'll be right back.

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:56.930
One is my world, it is who I am, it is what I am, I was once a man, I know the evil men do evil here, I warn you, beware the wrath of one thing.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.340
Come on, we gotta stop! We gotta find some cover!

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:04.860
There's not a part of me that's not facility!

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:05.860
Stop crying!

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:08.720
I put up with worse than this and non for two tours.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.640
Do me a favor, guys, just watch out for gators, okay?

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.560
Shut up, Zeepard! I'm sick of your gator story!

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.020
It's your own good, Mick!

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.660
Alligators don't need all that much water to hide in!

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.680
They just sit for hours, never moving!

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.670
Then they grab you!

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:24.580
Rollin' you over and over till you drown!

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:26.220
I told you we should've dumped him!

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:27.720
You calm down!

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.320
None of us are pleased about this!

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:32.340
That's when they eat you, you know, after you're drowned.

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:33.620
You know something, Seifert?

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.500
I'm real glad you told us about that because I'm gonna think about it

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.630
every time I buy alligator shoes.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.440
I'm gonna even check the tongue and see whose it is.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.340
Because if you don't shut up, it might be yours!

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:52.180
I'm gonna tell him what to do with a gator attack.

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:55.450
Don't let him bother you. You know how he did.

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:57.390
I'll tell you instead, okay, Joey?

00:04:57.390 --> 00:04:58.940
Yeah, sure. I'd appreciate it.

00:04:58.940 --> 00:04:59.540
Okay.

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:03.980
alligator attack. Remember, don't panic, they got this real soft spot right between

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:07.980
her eyes. So what you gotta do is, you just gotta keep jabbing him in the face like this.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:11.940
Okay? Hey, yeah, that's great, that's great. Mick's gonna be sorry he didn't know that.

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:23.410
Storm's got the dog spooked, but we're gonna press on. Ryzen's out of here someplace,

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:25.670
and I'm gonna bring him in.

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:38.170
Alright, look, that's it.

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:40.140
My legs are killing me. I gotta stop.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:44.300
I don't know which is worse, secrets, damn gator stories, or you're whining.

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:46.960
Well, I'm sorry we can't all be superheroes like you, Rycin.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:56.130
Suppose I could stand down.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.890
I don't hear no hounds anyway.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:11.950
great ain't it guys finally going for the money after all this time just being out of that cell

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:24.160
is enough for me what are you do with your cut mick well i sure as hell ain't gonna put it in no bank

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:37.730
I'm thinking of some drug business

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:40.340
Maybe get my own plane for some

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:42.640
High dollar hauls out of Columbia

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:45.320
How about you Joe? Are you going in with Mick?

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:48.590
Not a chance

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:50.920
I was never cut out for this

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:53.040
I'm out of it

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:12.770
think anybody is gonna let you go straight and escaped con all i need is a break you take it

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:22.500
from me the only break worth anything is the ones you make yourself how you gonna do it joey i'm

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:30.000
never gonna gamble again that's for sure i'm gonna put my energy into starting a small business

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:37.900
someplace just me and mary ellen oh gosh oh golly ozzy nelson lives what is your problem you you

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:43.580
don't get it that's what that heist that's the biggest jackpot you always wanted that's the daily

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:51.140
double of your dreams and all you can talk about is some fairy tale fantasy a small business well

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:59.070
not me this is my payday and they're all gonna pay you just can't stop blaming other people for

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:00.000
your problems huh

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.070
Oh, I forget. You didn't grow up in my neighborhood, did you?

00:08:04.070 --> 00:08:09.190
You had a family and a cushy life. You even went to college.

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:10.160
For a year.

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:13.120
Yeah. Well, that's a year more than they ever gave me.

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:17.030
I'll bet you even had one of those little sorority girls, didn't you?

00:08:17.030 --> 00:08:19.240
Some cheerleader in a tight sweater.

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:29.440
I'm gonna buy a good suit. Top quality.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:32.990
And then I'm going to Mitty's Tap on a Saturday night.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:35.590
Buy around for everybody.

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:39.660
Regulars used to make fun of me.

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:45.170
Like, just because I was a little slow that I was never going to make it big.

00:08:46.610 --> 00:08:47.130
They'll see.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.260
John Seifert's no loser.

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:05.000
I can't wait to see their faces when I walk in flashing a wad of hunters.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:16.300
You fellows are invited if you want to come.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:20.520
Sorry, Mr. Trump. I'm busy that night.

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:24.380
Anybody else hungry?

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:26.330
I could use something.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:29.280
Let's hope Ding Dong brought more than Gatorade.

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:36.160
Where's the pack, Seaford?

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:40.250
I don't know, Mick. I said it right here.

00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:42.090
Yeah, well, it sure as hell ain't here now.

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:43.890
What are you talking about? It has to be.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:44.810
It's gone.

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:46.900
Aw, you stupid moron!

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:49.320
Come on, Rycin!

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:52.170
I... Maybe Gator got it. They're real tricky.

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:54.470
Yeah, well, compared to you, a damn rock seems tricky.

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:55.270
Rycin, come on, listen!

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:55.960
No!

00:09:55.960 --> 00:09:57.290
I told you it was baggage.

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:57.780
Mick!

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:04.270
Come on, the dogs. They're on our sin again.

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:06.520
You want to lead them right to us?

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:53.480
I don't know about this.

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:55.310
What if there's more than one guy out there?

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:56.770
No, do you want to eat or not?

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.150
Not if it means we're walking into something here.

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:00.000
I'd rather find the food.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:00.640
someplace else.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:01.800
All right, all right.

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:04.360
Seifert, you lost our stuff,

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:06.040
so you're elected to check things out.

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:07.430
Sure thing, Mick.

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:08.490
It's the least I can do.

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:10.750
No, the least you could do is die,

00:11:10.830 --> 00:11:12.390
but I've kind of given up hope for that.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:25.350
You know, you really made me nervous before.

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:27.420
No, everything makes you nervous.

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:30.000
For a second there, I actually thought that

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:37.760
you were gonna kill don you never popped anybody before did you citrano you know what happened

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:45.920
well it kind of grows on you like back in um i never understood what the fuss was about over the

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:53.800
war because i kind of liked the killing and i got pretty good at it too so why didn't you stay in

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:59.060
the service huh you could have had a career because they were all against me

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:06.590
Good news. I saw snakes and frogs, but no campers or gators.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:09.560
Bear me, will you see for...

00:12:52.620 --> 00:13:00.000
your mind my god my god call psyops boys a little message to the enemy

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.760
to let them know who they're dealing with.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:03.420
But he was harmless, Mick.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:07.050
Nobody's harmless when you're on the run.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:08.330
Execute killers in this state.

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:09.330
Did you ever think of that?

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:10.330
Maybe you don't ever think.

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:13.260
Hey, college boy, I don't have to think.

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:15.040
I live by what my gut tells me,

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:17.100
and you don't want to know what it's saying right now.

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:18.020
I survived in prison.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:19.440
I can go the distance with you.

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:20.820
A promise is promise.

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:22.500
Push me, and I'll kill you, Ryzen.

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:23.620
That is a promise.

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:43.680
Okay, Seaford anchors away.

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:46.640
Get the boat in the water, I'm gonna get the rest of the supplies.

00:13:48.080 --> 00:13:49.520
I don't know, Mick.

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:51.560
You never know what could be in there.

00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:59.550
It was right here a minute ago.

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:00.000
I knew it!

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:01.250
Scream, where is he?

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:09.550
That's no concern

00:14:09.550 --> 00:14:11.830
What you want is

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:30.000
Citrano, maybe those bloodhounds

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:30.560
I missed it!

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:32.060
Come on, he's gotta be out there somewhere!

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:34.060
Let's face it, that guy is gator food!

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:35.060
Now let's move out!

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.400
We only got a few more clicks.

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:45.850
Please don't let the gators get me!

00:14:45.850 --> 00:14:46.850
You wanna live?

00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:48.000
Yes.

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:49.520
So did the fisherman.

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:57.360
I didn't know Mip was gonna kill him, honest!

00:14:57.360 --> 00:14:59.360
That didn't make it any easier for him to die.

00:15:02.490 --> 00:15:03.560
G-g-g-g-g!

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:05.700
You stole the money and a man died.

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:08.620
Now you must pay for what happened.

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:09.770
Go...

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:11.140
and do what's right.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:32.030
I can tell where Mick Wrightson is, please!

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:34.780
Please!

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:41.240
I'll be damned.

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:45.660
Listen, are you sure this is it?

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:47.710
Everything is totally submerged here.

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:53.240
We buried it here so the swamp would keep it covered.

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:58.400
Now, dig it.

00:15:58.400 --> 00:15:59.480
What's that for?

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:04.140
I'm beginning to think that a million dollars sounds twice as interesting as half a million.

00:16:04.420 --> 00:16:06.080
Come on, Ryzen, we were supposed to be partners!

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:07.500
Now we're history, now dig!

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:18.460
How am I supposed to dig in all this mud?

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:19.920
Like your life?

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:20.800
Depend it on.

00:16:54.350 --> 00:16:58.050
- I wasn't here.

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:00.000
- I saw the way you and Seifert took the death of that

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:02.850
Now maybe you two are looking to get even.

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:04.700
What are you talking about? Donnie is dead.

00:17:04.700 --> 00:17:07.890
No. Or maybe he's out there watching me.

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:09.890
Right now and he's waiting for an opening.

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:11.840
I'll put the knife away.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:15.240
Grayson, come on, if Donnie is behind us, he's in it alone!

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:17.240
No, no, he's too stupid to plan anything like this.

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:19.240
But then there's you!

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:21.240
You got a year of college!

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:23.240
McGrawl!

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:29.480
McGrawl!

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:59.380
I'm here for the money.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:09.240
gone it's over there I knew you stole the money but I didn't know where it was

00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:13.540
hidden I I never wanted to rob that armored car I was desperate I had bookies

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:16.770
I had to pay them off they were gonna hurt my wife the bank you robbed is in

00:18:16.770 --> 00:18:30.000
trouble innocent people are suffering I want that money returned

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:31.900
I give up. I give up.

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:36.770
You know it's not supposed to work like this?

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:38.390
But I ain't complaining.

00:18:38.850 --> 00:18:40.050
I'm up for a promotion.

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:47.870
You think you can trip me up?

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:50.670
You forget it, Citrano!

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:54.480
This is Mick Rice and you're dealing with!

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:58.270
You and see for nobody trips me up!

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:13.440
of my dreams. I was gonna do great things, but you let me down. You ruined everything.

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:28.220
But it wasn't my fault. They were all against me. What you doing, boy?

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:33.310
What's the matter with you?

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:35.280
What is it?

00:19:35.280 --> 00:19:37.490
What's the matter with you, Gabby?

00:19:37.490 --> 00:19:39.730
Gabby?

00:19:39.730 --> 00:19:55.410
What are you?

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:58.430
Where's my dog? Gabby?

00:19:58.430 --> 00:19:59.570
Come back!

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:01.560
He didn't know you anymore.

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:03.760
You were a different person back then.

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:06.600
This isn't happening.

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:08.420
I'm out of here.

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:10.800
It's not too late, Ryzen.

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:12.620
You can learn from your mistakes.

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:40.880
Why are you so jittery, Citrono?

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:42.390
It's just us.

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:45.120
You know, better than to jump somebody like that, Bryson.

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:49.040
Just keeping you on your toes, buddy boy. I need you razor sharp.

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:50.840
'Cause we're going tonight.

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:52.440
Since when?

00:20:52.440 --> 00:20:55.560
I think Storm's moving in, Joey.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:58.320
Nick says it'll make it harder for him to track us in the mud and all.

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:13.640
Count me out. I'm doing my time.

00:21:15.510 --> 00:21:17.730
Be a jerk. You waited a long time.

00:21:18.740 --> 00:21:21.460
Look, I can't explain it, but I got a real bad feeling about this whole thing.

00:21:21.830 --> 00:21:23.970
About the escape and that swamp.

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:27.960
You stay, you give up your share.

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:29.840
I'm sure you'll spend the money wisely.

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:33.610
Come on Seifert, let's hit it.

00:21:33.610 --> 00:21:36.420
I think I'm staying with Joey, Mick.

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:37.420
What's with you guys?

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:41.500
Thinking like that, that's gonna cost you more than 300 grand each.

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:42.480
What we did was wrong.

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:46.330
We don't deserve that money.

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:47.830
Suit yourself.

00:21:47.830 --> 00:21:50.420
See you around, chumps.

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:16.200
It's been said that those who do not learn from history are doomed to repeat it.

00:22:16.200 --> 00:22:19.940
Learning from the future is no less important.
